22 May 1777 (prov. 9 Jun 1777), will, Phillip Kissagger of Washington County, wife Margaretha - son John Nicholas - second son Simon - third son Philip - daughter Margaretha - daughter Agnes - witn. Henry Snibely + Nicholas Smith + Michael Hagar
6 Mar 1777 (prov. 9 Jun 1777), will, Alexander McClenochen farmer in Frederick County, wife Jean McClenochen - oldest son James McClenoghan - second son Alexander McClenoghan - daughter Elizabeth McClenoghan - daughter Jane McClenoghan - my son James McClenoghans daughter Jean - friend Dr. Robert Martin - witn. Robert Martin + John Workman + James McClannahan
4 Feb 1777 (prov. 14 Jun 1777), will, Andrew Putman of Washington County, wife Catharine - children: John + Peter + Elizabeth + mary + Mary Ann + Catharine + Susannah + Andrew - friends Samuel Baker and Conrad Shnebley exec. - witn. Henry Geeting + John William Tolts + Peter Shally
20 May 1777 (prov. 5 Jul 1777), will, George Househalter of Washington County, wife Margaret Househalter - three eldest sons Jacob Househalter + George Adam Househalter + George Michael Househalter - six youngest children viz. Margaret Househalter + Elizabeth Househalter + Catharine Househalter + Barbara Househalter + John George Househalter + John Househalter - brother Adam Househalter exec. - wit. Anthony Howard + George Neigh + Michael Househalter
24 Jun 1777 (prov. 15 Aug 1777), will, John Enderes of Masch Hundred upon Ringgolds Manor in Washington and province of Maryland, 
